# Never sent to the image build:
# - node_modules: the build installs its own, for Linux. Windows packages
#   (like Vite's native build tools) wouldn't run there anyway.
# - dist: the build creates a fresh one.
# - public/config.js and config.example.js: config.js is generated when the
#   container starts; neither belongs in the built site.
node_modules
dist
public/config.js
public/config.example.js
.env
.env.*
Dockerfile
.dockerignore